      {
        "title": "2. CONGENITAL &amp; LEUKOCORIA",
        "content": "• <b>Idiopathic:</b> 33%.<br>\n      • <b>Lamellar (Zonular):</b> AD, riders; Galactosemia, Hypocalcemia.<br>\n      • <b>Posterior Polar:</b> At <b>Nodal Point</b> $\\rightarrow$ severe vision drop!<br>\n      • <b>Leukocoria DD:</b> Cataract, Retinoblastoma (13q14), ROP, PHPV, Toxocara (🚫 <i>NOT Buphthalmos, Optic atrophy, or Choroidal melanoma!</i>).<br>\n      • <b>Rx:</b> Operate <b>immediately (at 2 wks)</b> to prevent <b>Amblyopia</b>!"
      },
      {
        "title": "3. SENILE &amp; SECONDARY",
        "content": "• <b>Nuclear:</b> Index myopia (\"Second sight\").<br>\n      • <b>Cortical:</b> Spoke-like; Mature = entire cortex opaque (HM vision).<br>\n      • <b>PSC:</b> Glare in bright sunlight/reading; caused by <b>Steroids (#1)</b>, Uveitis, High Myopia, RP.<br>\n      • <b>Specific:</b> <i>Snowflake</i> = Young Type 1 DM; <i>Shield</i> = Atopic dermatitis (10%); <i>Rosette</i> = Blunt trauma; <i>Sunflower</i> = Wilson's; <i>Granules</i> = Chlorpromazine."
      }
